From a93c7a3aa653c07c94ab0dd9e8c0cc59f3f45784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:50:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(animations): decode and transport native actor commands

Decode every field of protocol 2193 AnimateEntity packets, including the stop-expression version and unsigned runtime IDs. Resolve targets in core and publish current actor snapshots before sending lifetime-bound commands over a negotiated Java payload channel.

Keep authored animation, controller, transition, and blend values intact for native client integrations. Split large target groups into bounded payloads. Ordinary Java cannot faithfully execute arbitrary resource-defined bone commands, so transport requires both actor-state and animation capabilities.

Match the wire order against official Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372 captures and the protocol 2193 schema. Client controller playback and native timing comparisons remain separate required work.

Retain per-lifetime command controllers in the shared actor registry. Keep named next states, ordered transitions, native target/expression deduplication, and selection revisions without an ever-growing packet journal. Resource availability remains specific to each rendering context. Follow the target executable state builder and controller-update probes, including repeated selections and outgoing blend curves.
